{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794698013,"nonce":"1q3ejaDB8AnLq6irVEMw0Pvwm5E=","title":"hxn-gpu-metal: a Metal driver over the Apple frameworks, binding by hxnsl's slots","message":"The first of hxn-gpu's driver libraries. It wraps Metal directly through\nobjc2-metal rather than wgpu, so the MSL hxnsl writes is bound by the slots\nit reports and no wgpu-hal numbering has to be matched. No Naga is linked.\n\nWhy Metal first: Metal tracks resource hazards itself by default, so the\nbarrier tracking Vulkan and D3D12 need does not arise; shaders can be\nprecompiled to a metallib with `xcrun metal` when building on macOS, which\nalso removes the driver's MSL compile at run time, with MSL text as the\nfallback elsewhere.\n\nScope: device, buffers, textures and samplers, libraries from metallib or MSL,\nrender and compute pipeline states, command buffers and encoders, binding by\nslot, and presenting through a CAMetalLayer on the view hxn-window's raw()\nhandles give. macOS first, then iOS.\n\nDepends on hxnsl for its shaders.","files":null}]}